course: dictionary
lesson: 4455
title: Happily: more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Happily is an adverb. It tells you how something is done, and it often ends in -ly. Happy describes a thing or a person, as in «a happy girl». Happily describes an action, as in «chat happily».
explain: «A year later they bump into each other in town and chat happily for ten minutes.» Here happily means in a happy, cheerful way. Read the sentence again and ask: how do they chat? The answer is cheerfully, so happily fits.
explain: Happily can also mean willingly or gladly. «I'll happily help» means «I am glad to help». Happily can also mean luckily, as in «Happily, nobody was hurt.» Check the context. Swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Happily is an adverb, and it comes from the adjective happy.
fact: Happily can mean in a cheerful way: «They chat happily for ten minutes.»
fact: Happily can mean gladly or willingly: «I'll happily help.»
fact: Happily can mean luckily: «Happily, nobody was hurt.»
fact: Adverbs like happily, sadly and quickly show how something is done.
exercise: «A year later they bump into each other in town and chat happily for ten minutes.» How do they chat? | Crossly and in a hurry | Sadly, in tears | Silently, with no words at all | *In a cheerful, happy way
exercise: «Happily, nobody was hurt.» What does happily mean here? | Gladly, with a smile | Angrily | *Luckily | Quickly, before the crash
exercise: Ben says, «I'll happily help you with your maths.» What does he mean? | He will help only if he is paid | *He is glad and willing to help | He does not want to help at all | He will help next year
test: «There they find Taffy making daisy-chains and Tegumai happily spearing small carp.» What does happily mean here? | Carelessly, without looking | *Cheerfully, enjoying what he is doing | Sadly, after losing his spear | Slowly, with great effort
test: Which word is the adverb form of happy? | Happy-ness | *Happily | Happiness | Happier
exam: Which sentence uses happily to mean luckily? | *«Happily, the storm passed us by without harm.» | «She was a happy girl at school.» | «He was full of happiness.» | «The happy dog wagged its tail.»
